[{"id":79965,"sender_id":349,"sender_full_name":"bblfish","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/5d537347eb54566c1b9d975a30fc0147?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/What.20is.20ISP.3F.20.28used.20by.20Y.2E.20Maruyama.20in.20.22Natural.20duality.2C.20Moda.E2.80.A6/near/79965\">#1</a> In “<a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0022404911001666?via%3Dihub\">Natural duality, Modality, and Coalgebras</a>”, in his thesis <a href=\"http://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/people/bob.coecke/Yoshi.pdf\">Meaning and Duality - From Categorical Logic to Quantum Physics</a>, and elsewhere <a href=\"https://researchmap.jp/ymaruyama\">Yoshihiro Maruyama</a> talks about <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{ISP}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">ISP</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{ISP}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">ISP</span></span></span></span></span>(M), how it is composed of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{I}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathrm\">I</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{S}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathrm\">S</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{P}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathrm\">P</span></span></span></span>, but I can’t figure out what these stand for.</p>","timestamp":1574460238,"subject":"What is ISP? (used by Y. Maruyama in \"Natural duality, Moda…","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":79968,"sender_id":349,"sender_full_name":"bblfish","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/5d537347eb54566c1b9d975a30fc0147?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/What.20is.20ISP.3F.20.28used.20by.20Y.2E.20Maruyama.20in.20.22Natural.20duality.2C.20Moda.E2.80.A6/near/79968\">#2</a> I got the answer on <a href=\"https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/3447447/what-kind-of-structure-is-an-isp/3447462#3447462\">StackExchange</a> and was actually just about to find the answer myself. What is missing in Maruyama’s thesis wa